title: munir_topic_character_to_player_first_contact
tags: actor:Munir actor:Prince
---
Munir: *Assalamu alaikum, young man.*  
Munir: You seem a little lost. Can I help you with something?  

Prince: Uh… yeah.  
Prince: I’m lookin’ for a man named Munir.  
Prince: Tall dude, supposed to be here.  

Munir: *Wa alaikum assalam.*  
Munir: Then you have found him.  
Munir: I am Munir ibn Aziz Al-Askar.  
Munir: And who might you be?  

Prince: Name’s Prince.  
Prince: Mister Hariri told me to come find you.  
Prince: Said you run this place.  

Munir: *Ah… Hariri.*  
Munir: He mentioned you, yes.  
Munir: You were both at the hospital, right?  

Prince: Yeah.
-> Prince: I planned to kill Oldboy and Buddy during our last burglary. <<if false>>
-> Prince: It didn't go as planned, I chased Oldboy and Buddy throughout the city. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I caught up to them and got into a fight<<if false>>
-> Prince: I struck Oldboy in the head. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I strangled Buddy with my hands. <<if false>>
-> Prince: My heart stopped and I dropped Buddy on the ground. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I don't know how I ended up in the hospital. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I wanted to die. <<if false>>
-> Prince: Just say it wasn't the best week.
Prince: Wasn’t my best week.  
Prince: They said my heart’s messed up.  
Prince: Real bad.  

Munir: *I’m sorry to hear that.*  
Munir: I also had surgery once, years ago.  
Munir: It humbles a man.  
Munir: How are you feeling now?  

Prince: Physically?  
Prince: Like I’m wearin’ bricks under my ribs.  
Prince: Mentally? 
-> Prince: I want to die. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I'm stressed out of my mind <<if false>>
-> Prince: I feel like I'm drowning. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I don't know.
Prince: …I don’t know.  
Prince: I guess that’s why I’m here.  

Munir: You came to the masjid seeking peace, then.  
Munir: Many do.  
Munir: What troubles you, Prince?  

-> Prince: I'm a seventeen year old kid with no family, no home, and no future. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I'm a thief and a liar, and I don't know how to stop. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I have no idea what I'm doing with my life. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I have 20 kids depending on me to keep them safe and fed. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I'm scared all the time, and I don't know why. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I struck the head of my closest friend and strangled his 10 year old brother. <<if false>>
-> Prince: I have a failing heart and only have 2 years left to live. <<if false>>
-> Prince: Lot's of things.

Prince: *Heh.*  
Prince: Lotta things, old man.  
Prince: But mostly—  
Prince: …I got people who depend on me.  

Munir: Family?  

Prince: Sorta.  
Prince: A group of kids.  
Prince: We call ourselves the Alley Cats.
Prince: We...
-> Prince: Steal from warehouses. <<if false>>
-> Prince: Pickpocket. <<if false>>
-> Prince: Steal from shops. <<if false>>
-> Prince: Conceal and lie to Munir about what you do.
Prince: We… stick together.  
Prince: Help each other out.  
Prince: Some of us sell scrap, some run errands for shops, some fix stuff.  
Prince: Just tryna make ends meet, you know?  

Munir: *Masha’Allah.*  
Munir: That is noble of you.  
Munir: But I can sense something behind your tone.  
Munir: You’re afraid for them, aren’t you?  

Prince: Yeah.  
Prince: Afraid they’ll end up worse than me.  
Prince: Afraid I’ll die before I can fix anything.  
Prince: …Afraid I’ll leave ‘em stranded.  
Prince: I want ‘em safe.  
Prince: I want ‘em clean.  
Prince: I want ‘em to live longer than me.  
Prince: Maybe even smile without thinkin’ about tomorrow’s dinner.  

Munir: Then perhaps that is why Allah brought you here.  
Munir: Hariri said you were interested in Islam.  

Prince: I mean—yeah, a bit.  
Prince: Don’t know where to start, though.  
Prince: I ain’t the book type.  

Munir: No one begins with books.  
Munir: They begin with the heart.  
Munir: If you wish, we can talk each day after Asr prayer.  
Munir: Slowly. Patiently.  
Munir: I will not rush you.  

Prince: You serious? You’d do that for me?  

Munir: Of course.  
Munir: Guidance is not mine to give or withhold.  
Munir: I am only a gardener.  
Munir: I tend to the soil. The rest belongs to Allah.  

Prince: *Heh.*  
Prince: You talk fancy.  
Prince: But… I get it.  
Prince: I’ll come by.  

Munir: Good.  
Munir: And if your heart feels heavy again, Prince—  
Munir: Remember that even stone can bloom when it meets rain.  

Prince: …That’s deep.  
Prince: You got more lines like that?  

Munir: *Plenty.*  
Munir: But you will have to earn them by showing up tomorrow.  

Prince: Heh. Aight, old man.  
Prince: You got yourself a deal.  

Munir: Then it’s settled.  
Munir: Welcome, Prince.  
Munir: May this place be a refuge for you and those you love.  

Prince: Yeah.  
Prince: Thanks.  
Prince: …Guess I’ll see you tomorrow, then.  

Munir: Insha’Allah.  
Munir: Go in peace, son.  

Prince: Peace, huh?  
Prince: We’ll see.

